---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title="VoltUI capabilities" titleEn="VoltUI capabilities" titleZh="VoltUI 能力" description="The current VoltUI Electron and official DeepSeek Harness capability boundary.">
  <SiteHeader active="capabilities" />
  <main class="wrap"><section class="page-hero"><div class="eyebrow">CAPABILITIES / 能力</div><h1>Official DSH capabilities, presented through a focused Electron shell.</h1><p>Session state, tools, approvals, workspace access, plugins and credentials stay inside the official runtime. VoltUI keeps the host boundary small and inspectable.</p></section><section class="home-section"><div class="grid"><article class="feat"><div class="n">01</div><h3>Sessions</h3><p>Persisted conversations and recovery are owned by the DSH web profile.</p><code>DSH_HOME/sessions</code></article><article class="feat"><div class="n">02</div><h3>Tools and MCP</h3><p>Use the official tool and MCP bundles with DSH permission policies.</p><code>.mcp.json</code></article><article class="feat"><div class="n">03</div><h3>Workspace</h3><p>Launch from the selected local workspace and keep the shell bound to loopback.</p><code>DSH_WORKSPACE</code></article><article class="feat"><div class="n">04</div><h3>Model profiles</h3><p>Apply the repository profile patch while preserving the official bundle graph.</p><code>profiles/anyong.yml</code></article><article class="feat"><div class="n">05</div><h3>Security boundary</h3><p>Sandboxed BrowserWindow, denied popups, origin allowlist and managed child cleanup.</p><code>contextIsolation: true</code></article><article class="feat"><div class="n">06</div><h3>Packaging</h3><p>Electron-builder unpacks the official DSH tree for the child process and emits Windows x64 review artifacts.</p><code>pnpm run dist:desktop</code></article></div></section><section class="band"><h2>Operate one runtime with evidence.</h2><p>See the deployment and verification contract before distributing a build.</p><a class="btn btn-dark" href={base + '/enterprise/'}>Deployment guide</a></section></main><SiteFooter />
</Base>
